# Checkpoint QA

## Status: paused (Jul 23, 2026)

**Do not run** the mandatory pre-freeze QA pass (mock server, full-game exercise, playing-layout captures / class V diffs) unless the user explicitly asks for QA.

Reason: screenshot hash diffs were noisy (capture noise → constant “changed” → promote anyway) and did **not** catch the UI regressions that matter (pixel shifts, avatar sizing, etc.). User playtesting is the gate for now.

Checkpoints / deploys proceed per `checkpoints.mdc` and `deploy.mdc` **without** waiting on this file.

## Optional (only if user asks)

Port safety if you do start a mock QA server: prefer free port; prefer **4000 + mock** when 3000 is busy; never kill a process you did not start; if both busy, ask.

Helper (kept, not required): `node qa/capture-playing-layouts.js` → `qa/visual-baselines/_pending/`. Baselines under `qa/visual-baselines/<date>/` remain historical reference only.

### Class checklist (reference if QA is re-enabled)

**A — Animations & transitions** — timed overlays hold full life; Video on ≥ clip; no early advance; dismiss → playing clean.

**B — Cross-game consistency** — next-player / winner / Control actions feel consistent.

**C — Core functionality** — roster/start/score/undo/sync; Video toggle.

**V — Playing-layout visuals** — capture vs latest baseline; unexpected drift → fail (was required; currently paused).

**D — Regression classes** — _None yet._
